e="1" parent="1" source="dp_exit" target="idle"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" x="0.85"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="22" y="1667" /><mxPoint x="22" y="470" /><mxPoint x="100" y="470" /></Array><mxPoint x="14.0" y="0.0" as="offset" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="f_deposit" value="B1 | wheeldrop" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;endSize=7;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.25;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#b85450;labelBackgroundColor=none;align=center;exitX=0.2703;exitY=0.0000;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.1356;entryY=1.0000;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="dp_phase" target="fault"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" x="0.9"><mxPoint x="55.0" y="0.0" as="offset" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_dot" value="" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="44" y="2026" width="16" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_dot_t" value="start (initial State)" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="2026" width="150" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_dia" value="" style="rhombus;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="230" y="2020" width="28" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_dia_t" value="choice: one trigger, the guard on each edge picks the way" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="266" y="2026" width="340" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_st" value="state" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="2020" width="90" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_fa" value="fault" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="750" y="2020" width="90" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_su" value="composite (sub-FSM)" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="2020" width="170" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lg_red" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#b85450&quot;&gt;red edge&lt;/font&gt; = fault: the State leaves for STOP / FAULT" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1290" y="2026" width="560" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="note1" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A State is a rounded box: its name, then its actions. &lt;b&gt;entry /&lt;/b&gt; runs once on entering, &lt;b&gt;do /&lt;/b&gt; on every Tick in which no edge fired, &lt;b&gt;exit /&lt;/b&gt; once on leaving. Edges read: trigger [guard] / effect. A State's edges are checked in priority order and the first true one fires; a transition runs exit(), then the effect, then entry() of the next State.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;ε&lt;/b&gt; = no trigger: the edge is taken on the next Tick. One Tick = one Kobuki packet: Kobuki_Read() runs first, then the state switch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Angles are degrees: + = ACW (left), - = CW (right) (Kobuki_Rotate: +ve is CCW). &lt;b&gt;heading&lt;/b&gt; = kobuki.angle, latched at the start of each corridor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Setpoints (Kobuki_Rotate_Angle_Setpoint, Kobuki_Drive_Distance_Setpoint) are one-shot entry actions. kobuki.rotation_complete and kobuki.distance_complete are copied at the top of the Tick, so a State sees them one Tick after its last do / call." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2076" width="570" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="note2" value="&lt;b&gt;Layouts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A / B is the Layout saved by IDENTIFY, never a live reading. Layout A: bollards A1/A2 block the left/top route, so the AMU takes the bottom corridor, then the right corridor; the storage wall is on its left and the ledge on its right. Layout B is the mirror image: bollards B1/B2 block the bottom/right route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sensors&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bumper / cliff bits: right = 0x01, centre = 0x02, left = 0x04. B0 = kobuki.button &amp; 0x01 (start). B1 = kobuki.button &amp; 0x02 (stop). wheeldrop = kobuki.wheeldrop != 0.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Faults&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The sensor fault edge is the first edge of its State, so it wins. B1 | wheeldrop leaves every State except IDLE. The SEARCH phase States and ORIENT also fault on any bumper or cliff. Bumpers and cliffs are expected in PATHFIND, STORAGE and DEPOSIT, so those regions have one red edge each, for B1 | wheeldrop only. The SEARCH give-up is the only fault timeout: it faults with LED1 green when it finds nothing. DEPOSIT never gives up; its only limit is 5 DEPOSIT_BACKOFFs, after which MEASURE ends in IDLE." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="2076" width="570" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="note3" value="&lt;b&gt;Constants (Src/Helper/helper.h)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;path speed 150, reverse 50 mm, wall-hit nudge A -5 / B +5 (ledge cliff: the opposite), corner A +90 / B -90, Orient A -75 / B +103, storage turn A +135 / B -135, drive-in 900 mm. Scan: turn speed 150, give-up after a full turn of 360. Layout split 575 mm (B below, A otherwise). Detect range 750 mm (Src/Ultrasonic/ultrasonic.h).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Helpers (Src/Helper/helper.c)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Layout_From_Range(range_mm) is the single split. Scan_Start() zeroes the scan; Scan_Update_Turn() adds the gyro change to scan_deg. Scan_Sample() and Scan_Gave_Up() are in the same file, with Fault_B1_Wheeldrop(), Fault_Any(), Layout_Pick() and the Corridor_Take_* checks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;IDLE reset&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;IDLE clears the layout, object, heading, corridor and scan variables when B0 starts a run.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Calibration (layout split, detect range)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The split is a calibration value (575 mm now). IDENTIFY reads the first in-range reading, taken as the sonar beam first reaches the bollard, so calibrate the same way: turn the AMU anticlockwise onto B1, then onto A1, and read robot.object.range_mm when SEARCH stops; the split goes between them. The detect range must stay above the A1 reading and below the nearest wall." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1240" y="2076" width="570" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>